.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/recruiting/story/_/id/38895893/how-top-50-2023-recruits-done-college-freshmen","type":"Story","byline":"Blake Baumgartner and Tom VanHaaren","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Five-star safety Peyton Bowen flips again, now off to Oklahoma","description":"Five-star safety prospect Peyton Bowen, who previously flipped his commitment from Notre Dame to Oregon, has flipped once again, signing with Oklahoma Sooners, he announced on Twitter on Thursday.","published":"2024-01-23T16:02:06.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/35306416/five-star-safety-peyton-bowen-flips-again-now-oklahoma","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Blake Baumgartner","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Five-star safety Peyton Bowen flips from Notre Dame to Oregon","description":"Five-star safety Peyton Bowen, the No. 14 overall prospect in the 2023 ESPN 300, has flipped his commitment from Notre Dame to Oregon on national signing day.","published":"2024-01-15T20:32:55.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/35298055/five-star-safety-peyton-bowen-flips-notre-dame-oregon","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Blake Baumgartner","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Oklahoma coach Venables shouts out Love's after Buc-ee's comment","description":"Venables showed love Sunday to Buc-ee's -- which is owned by an alumnus of the Sooners' next opponent, Texas A&M. So on Tuesday the coach repped the Oklahoma-based Love's.","published":"2026-11-17T22:23:36.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50513199/oklahoma-brent-venables-loves-travel-stop","type":"Story","byline":"J.J. Post","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 college football coaching carousel: Tracking every open job","description":"As the carousel spins, we'll keep you updated with all the comings and goings.","published":"2026-11-17T21:26:31.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50358611/2026-cfb-coaching-carousel-firings-hirings","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"North Texas QB Tayven Jackson out with upper-body injury","description":"North Texas senior quarterback Tayven Jackson, who is sixth in the FBS with 3,005 passing yards, will miss at least the next two games with an upper-body injury.","published":"2026-11-17T20:53:17.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50513204/north-texas-qb-tayven-jackson-upper-body-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Defiant Dabo Swinney says Clemson's 'gonna win a bunch more'","description":"Despite going through a self-described \"rough patch\" over the past two seasons, Clemson coach Dabo Swinney is resolute in his belief that he and the Tigers have a lot more wins ahead of them.","published":"2026-11-17T20:37:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50512833/defiant-dabo-swinney-says-clemson-gonna-win-bunch-more","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Army OC Cody Worley to be Furman head coach","description":"Army offensive coordinator Cody Worley is expected to be the next head coach at Furman, sources told ESPN.","published":"2026-11-17T20:11:06.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50512672/army-oc-worley-furman-head-coach","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Former Iowa State AD calls NIL system 'money laundering'","description":"Former Iowa State athletic director Jamie Pollard delivered a scorching appraisal of college athletics to the Knight Commission, equating NIL as a money-laundering operation.","published":"2026-11-17T19:08:48.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-sports/story/_/id/50512485/former-iowa-state-ad-calls-nil-system-money-laundering","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Purdue rolls with FAA ground stop by taking buses to Iowa","description":"Unable to travel by plane, the Boilermakers rolled with the situation and found some good times on the way.","published":"2026-11-17T11:28:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50504665/purdue-faa-ground-stop-bus-iowa","type":"Story","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4870625/peyton-bowen","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peyton_Bowen"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Peyton Bowen","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peyton_Bowen","description":"American football cornerback (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:34:50Z","intro":"Peyton Bowen (born March 1, 2004) is an American college football safety for the Oklahoma Sooners.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Bowen grew up in Denton, Texas. He attended and played high school football at John H. Guyer High School. He intercepted 12 passes and broke up 23 passes in three varsity seasons at Guyer.\n\nRECRUITMENT\nBowen was rated a five-star recruit by ESPN and initially committed Notre Dame over offers from Alabama, Oklahoma, and USC. He later flipped his commitment from Notre Dame to Oregon. However, the following day Bowen changed his commitment a second time and signed his National Letter of Intent to play at Oklahoma. He later explained that his decision was due to a paperwork issue as Oregon had not sent him a letter of intent to sign before the start of the early signing period."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Bowen joined the Oklahoma Sooners as an early enrollee in January 2023. He entered the season as the team's second-string safety."}],"family":[{"relation":"Sibling","name":"Eli Bowen","description":"American football player","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eli_Bowen_(American_football)"}]}}